.Dd July 11, 2026
.Dt ZDOTS-STATUSD-CTL 8
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm zdots-statusd-ctl
.Nd manage the zdots.localhost control-plane status service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
controls
.Xr zdots-statusd 8 ,
the Observable Control Plane's own health console served at zdots.localhost.
It is deliberately separate from my.localhost (context-engine) so platform
health stays reachable when the Rails app or Postgres is down. The service is a thin viewer
over the zdots health tools
.Pq Xr zdots-ctl 8 , Xr zsvc 8 , service logs ;
the intelligence lives in those CLIs.
.Pp
The service binds loopback only on 127.0.0.1:${ZDOTS_STATUS_PORT:-11600};
.Xr nginx 8
terminates TLS for https://zdots.localhost. No secrets touch the launchd plist.
Manage it via
.Ic zsvc Ar verb Cm status ;
this script is the authoritative ctl backing that.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width restart
.It Cm install
Register the macOS launchd service (KeepAlive, RunAtLoad).
.It Cm start
Load and start the service.
.It Cm stop
Unload and stop the service.
.It Cm restart
Stop then start.
.It Cm status Op Fl -json
Show service state and process info.
.It Cm health Op Fl -json
Exit 0 if the service answers /healthz, 1 otherwise.
.It Cm logs
Tail the service log.
.It Cm run
launchd entry point: set up env, exec the HTTP server. Internal; not for
interactive use.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_STATUS_PORT
.It Ev ZDOTS_STATUS_PORT
Listen port (default 11600).
.It Ev ZDOTDIR
zdots root, for shelling out to zdots-ctl / zsvc.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.zdots.statusd.plist"
.It Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.zdots.statusd.plist
launchd agent definition (generated by
.Cm install Ns ).
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/zsh/zdots-statusd.log
Service log.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zdots-statusd 8 ,
.Xr zsvc 8 ,
.Xr zdots-ctl 8
